    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/cjvnjde/chatgpt-english-mcp/commit/63558e93df8d062b72f89b54b94e3fa2f669e7b9"/>
    <title>
        feat(admin): streamline the learning workspace
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-11T12:58:21Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68147661?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>cjvnjde</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/cjvnjde</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat(admin): streamline the learning workspace

Land on an actionable overview with daily activity and words needing attention. Simplify table filters and date selection, add sortable sticky headers and compact rows, and visualize next-draw probabilities without changing scheduler behavior.

Keep database tools available behind advanced controls and collapse navigation on mobile. Add date/summary/probability unit tests and an optional fixture browser regression suite.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/eb641fe2bd9eaeb7918d483e3d1c05c1d43cc1f0</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/cjvnjde/chatgpt-english-mcp/commit/eb641fe2bd9eaeb7918d483e3d1c05c1d43cc1f0"/>
    <title>
        fix: keep admin navigation and conflict decisions consistent
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-11T11:09:29Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68147661?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>cjvnjde</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/cjvnjde</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;fix: keep admin navigation and conflict decisions consistent

Traverse existing browser history without rewriting it, restore the current entry on draft cancellation, and invalidate superseded navigation decisions before they can corrupt route state.

Merge descriptions and their attribution as one conflict unit while preserving independent metadata edits. Make conflict alerts readable on small screens, improve navigation label contrast, and correct obsolete grading help.

Add regression tests for Back/Forward, cancelled and superseded confirmations, and atomic description/source decisions. Verify the production UI on desktop and mobile, including conflict persistence and accessibility scans.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/db865f958ec82bdd8f64d8bc839fe798c36d0548</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/cjvnjde/chatgpt-english-mcp/commit/db865f958ec82bdd8f64d8bc839fe798c36d0548"/>
    <title>
        fix: preserve vocabulary identity and reject unsafe text
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-11T11:09:17Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68147661?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>cjvnjde</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/cjvnjde</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;fix: preserve vocabulary identity and reject unsafe text

Return the exact saved item ID from learning_next and keep selected-sense save retries idempotent across dictionary refreshes and parser changes.

Reject NUL in exported vocabulary fields and malformed raw UTF-8 before admin or MCP JSON decoding can replace it. Preserve existing authentication, body limits, immutable snapshots, and transactional creation behavior.

Add regressions for overlapping senses, stale dictionary retries, invalid inputs, and unchanged storage after rejection. Document deliberate repair of legacy NUL records and current grading behavior.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
